    "answer": {
      "short": "Correct answer: C.",
      "worked": "Use the observed relative frequency to estimate the probability of rolling a 6.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Relative frequency of 6} &= \\frac{450}{1200}\\\\\\text{Relative frequency of 6} &= \\frac{3}{8}\\\\\\text{Remaining estimated probability} &= 1-\\frac{3}{8}\\\\\\text{Remaining estimated probability} &= \\frac{5}{8}\\\\\\text{Estimated probability of each other number} &= \\frac{5}{8}\\div5\\\\\\text{Estimated probability of each other number} &= \\frac{1}{8}\\\\\\text{Frequency ratio} &= \\frac{3}{8}\\div\\frac{1}{8}\\\\\\text{Frequency ratio} &= 3\\end{align*}$$\nThe number 6 is expected to appear 3 times as often as any one other number.\nCorrect answer: C.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
